-> Introduction to Linear Regression:
Linear regression is a statistical method used to establish a relationship between a dependent variable (target) and one or more independent variables (predictors). The primary goal is to predict the value of the target variable based on the predictor variables.

-> Types of Linear Regression:
i) Simple Linear Regression: Involves one independent variable.
Formula:
    y = mx+c 

Where:
y = predicted value (dependent variable)
m = slope of the regression line
x = independent variable
c = y-intercept

